WEBVTT

00:01:59.905 --> 00:02:03.566
So it's everywhere,
and we need to know how to exploit it.

00:02:04.069 --> 00:02:06.046
Well, let's go hand by hand

00:02:06.070 --> 00:02:09.276
and browse through just a few examples.

00:02:09.300 --> 00:02:10.815
What is a pest?

00:02:10.839 --> 00:02:14.149
What damage does it actually
inflict on the plant?

00:02:14.173 --> 00:02:16.434
And what is the natural enemy,

00:02:16.458 --> 00:02:19.441
the biological control agent,
or the "good bug"

00:02:19.465 --> 00:02:20.666
that we're talking about?

00:02:20.690 --> 00:02:25.703
In general, I'm going to talk
about insects and spiders,

00:02:25.727 --> 00:02:27.950
or mites, let us call them.

00:02:27.974 --> 00:02:30.743
Insects, those six-legged organisms